      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1356080
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-13T01:38:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "And how do users disable MTE?",
      "parentUuid": "f47402d1_a6950e5b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 47,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "f83956b9a9f48e0a5f76eda727c69861718b87aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f112fae_a9275ca8",
        "filename": "res/xml/development_settings.xml",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1268571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-13T05:26:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t intend it to show it in this option. A switch would give the wrong impression that this stays enabled until turned off, while this is a one off switch to reboot, and enable MTE for this one session.\n\nCurrently, we have two ideas, either\n\na) in DAC, tell people to use sanitizer-status from the command line to verify the reboot turned on MTE, or\nb) have a persistent notification that tells people that this is enabled.\n\nTo disable, users need to reboot again.\n\nThis approach was taken because this is an experimental configuration, and we want to make sure that it isn\u0027t accidentally turned on for longer than intended.",
      "parentUuid": "f47402d1_a6950e5b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 47,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "f83956b9a9f48e0a5f76eda727c69861718b87aa",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
